From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: serial: mediatek,uart: add MT6897 and the pad mode register

The MediaTek MT6897 (Dimensity 8300) UARTs work like those of the other
MediaTek SoCs, so add MT6897 with mediatek,mt6577-uart as the fallback.

SoCs of this generation have a UART hub in front of one of the UARTs,
UART3 on MT6897. A register in the pericfg_ao block routes that UART to
the hub or to its pads, and nothing comes out of the pads in hub mode.
All four UARTs share a compatible, so the compatible does not tell which
one has this mux. Add a property on that UART that points at the register.
MT6897 boards do not use the hub: its node in the MediaTek device trees
says uarthub-disable, and the Lenovo TB375FC has its keyboard cover on
the pads of UART3.

The syscon and the offset follow mediatek,syscon-wakeup of the MediaTek
USB bindings.

---
 .../bindings/serial/mediatek,uart.yaml        | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/mediatek,uart.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/mediatek,uart.yaml
index 5bd8a88..67d3f06 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/mediatek,uart.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/mediatek,uart.yaml
@@ -11,6 +11,15 @@ maintainers:
 
 allOf:
   - $ref: serial.yaml#
+  - if:
+      not:
+        properties:
+          compatible:
+            contains:
+              const: mediatek,mt6897-uart
+    then:
+      properties:
+        mediatek,syscon-pad-mode: false
 
 description: |
   The MediaTek UART is based on the basic 8250 UART and compatible
@@ -35,6 +44,7 @@ properties:
               - mediatek,mt6795-uart
               - mediatek,mt6797-uart
               - mediatek,mt6893-uart
+              - mediatek,mt6897-uart
               - mediatek,mt7622-uart
               - mediatek,mt7623-uart
               - mediatek,mt7629-uart
@@ -91,6 +101,17 @@ properties:
       - const: uart
       - const: wakeup
 
+  mediatek,syscon-pad-mode:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle-array
+    description:
+      On SoCs with a UART hub, one UART reaches either its pads or the hub,
+      as selected by a register in the pericfg_ao block. Given on that UART
+      to use it on its pads.
+    items:
+      - items:
+          - description: The pericfg_ao syscon
+          - description: The offset of the register
+
   pinctrl-0: true
   pinctrl-1: true
 
